      "text": "The route links Bogotá, Medellín, Pereira’s coffee region, Santa Marta, a four-day trek to the Lost City, Cartagena and the Rosario Islands. In Bogotá, you’ll visit La Candelaria, the Gold Museum, the Botero Museum and the underground Salt Cathedral of Zipaquirá. In Medellín, the itinerary takes in squares, parks, the cable car and Comuna 13. You’ll then visit the Cocora Valley and a coffee farm, head to the Caribbean coast, trek through the mountain territory of the Tayrona and spend the final days in Cartagena."
    },
